ters</p> <ul> <li>Chapter 26: Two Port Networks</li> </ul> <p>Appendices</p> <ul> <li>Appendix A: Circuit Functions</li> <li>Appendix B: Phasor Arithmetic</li> <li>Appendix C: Decibels</li> <li>Appendix D: Resources</li> </ul>"},{"location":"open-textbooks/wb-circuit-theory/index.html#about-this-book","title":"About this book","text":"<p>A university-level course in electric circuit theory: the basic laws and elements, resistive circuits and network theorems, energy-storing elements and first and second-order responses, phasors and AC power, frequency response and filters, Laplace-domain analysis and two-port networks.</p> <p>From Wikibooks · CC BY-SA 4.0</p><p>Circuit Theory, a Wikibooks textbook, by its contributors. This book is not stored in this library: each chapter is read from Wikibooks when it is opened, shown in this library's format, and ends with its own attribution. Licence: CC BY-SA 4.0. Modified: converted to this format.</p>"},{"location":"open-textbooks/wb-circuit-theory/1st-order-filters.html","title":"Chapter 20: 1st Order Filters","text":""},{"location":"open-textbooks/wb-circuit-theory/analysis-methods.html","title":"Chapter 8: Analysis Methods","text":""},{"location":"open-textbooks/wb-circuit-theory/analysis-methods.html#81-analysis-methods","title":"8.1 Analysis Methods","text":""},{"location":"open-textbooks/wb-circuit-theory/analysis-methods.html#82-superposition","title":"8.2 Superposition","text":""},{"location":"open-textbooks/wb-circuit-theory/analysis-methods.html#necessary-conditions","title":"Necessary Conditions","text":""},{"location":"open-textbooks/wb-circuit-theory/analysis-methods.html#step-by-step","title":"Step by Step","text":""},{"location":"open-textbooks/wb-circuit-theory/analysis-methods.html#83-impulse-response","title":"8.3 Impulse Response","text":""},{"location":"open-textbooks/wb-circuit-theory/analysis-methods.html#84-convolution","title":"8.4 Convolution","text":""},{"location":"open-textbooks/wb-circuit-theory/an